WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.900
This is heaven.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.480
I'm glad we got lost.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.980
It's so pretty here...

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.650
We never would've seen this beautiful scenery if we didn't get lost.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:17.200
Ai, please look at the map more carefully from now on, 'kay?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.160
Yeah...

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.410
And Yukina, please try not to get separated. It's really hard to find you.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.410
'Kay...

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.420
We're supposed to be in Kyoto right now...

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.920
This isn't so bad. It's not like we're in a hurry.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.840
We <i>are</i> in a hurry. The client is waiting for us, you know?

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.180
Well, they might be waiting for that Maccha person...

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.100
Substitutes can help too, if they try.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.020
Nagoya went well, didn't it?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.150
Maybe.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.820
I suppose Yukina's weird shachihoko helped a bit.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.320
Weird shachihoko?

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.240
Anyway, why'd you give back the stone we broke our backs over for?

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.950
I couldn't take that... It seemed like it was really important to her.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:07.370
Of course it was important! It's a stone that lets people become Bests!

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.090
You'll never get any if you keep thinking like that!

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.090
I think that might be fine, too.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:19.600
The President of Tokorozawa doesn't know that we're working as Masami's substitutes, anyway.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.180
Hey, I'm only here because I want one of those stones!

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.930
Really?

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.480
I told you, didn't I?

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.520
First, we get the ones for Chi,
then I'll get one of the leftovers.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.740
Nozomi, your first client was Chiaya.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.490
Oh yeah, that's right!

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.700
I-I wouldn't forget that!

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.120
Don't need 'em.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.120
I don't need 'em anymore.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:55.210
You don't? Are you sure?

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.050
The deer like her, huh?

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.350
I'll help Nonsuke.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.680
With Yukippe and Uu!

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.600
Th-Thanks...

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:16.440
You should use the next one, Nozomi.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.360
Huh?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.320
If you become a Best, it'll be easier for you to take that Maccha person's place.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:26.450
Huh? Uh, but I... I don't really want to...

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.420
Let's go!

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:45.140
When you're kicked around and rejected

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.890
Don't huddle in a corner on the days you're worn out

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.440
While singing...

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.190
The Moonlight Stone, huh?

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.910
If only one fell from the sky for Ai, too...

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.120
Nonsuke.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.210
Hm?

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:19.510
Will Uu go away once she finds a stone?

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.670
Probably...

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.390
But I wonder why she wants to be a Best so badly?

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.890
It looks like a bunch of pain and effort.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.850
Yukina, you don't want a stone?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.940
Not really...

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.730
I am a little curious about them, though.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.280
Then, why are you traveling with Nozomi?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.280
Huh?! Th-That's because...

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.330
I want more experience so I can make my dream come true...

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.180
I'm going to turn off the light.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.140
Oh, okay.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.220
Uu's asleep already.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.480
I feel like I'm going crazy

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:20.280
I like nice songs

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.700
and I want you to listen to them too

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.370
Whenever

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:35.330
I sing a song

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.920
I hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.380
wishing me the best

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.090
I want you

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.630
to hear it too

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.510
Good luck!

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.640
You can't show your love

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.140
just with niceties

00:04:56.140 --> 00:05:01.070
That won't provide comfort

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.400
Whenever I say something

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.490
out of the ordinary

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.830
in my heart

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.330
I wish you the best

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.880
I want you

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.500
to hear that line

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.460
Good luck!

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.150
The holy land of rock, Kyoto.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:50.450
This city has gone beyond its centuries of history and tradition to fuse with the beat.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.240
Now, many young people gather here.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.160
The echoes of the screams of their souls fill the air.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:16.470
Order is kept by two wildly different vigilante squads.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.980
The live concerts held at the famous old temples are operated and policed by the Kamogawa Rockr's.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:27.490
The peace of the old capital and its surrounding areas is kept by the veteran vigilante squad, Maikos, We are.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:31.110
The two groups bear these responsibilities completely separately.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.180
Give Me the Stars

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.550
Ah, you must be Maccha Green!
Give Me the Stars

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:54.750
Kiyomizu Temple
Rock Explosion
Security HQ
Ah, you must be Maccha Green!
Give Me the Stars

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.560
Ah, you must be Maccha Green!
Kiyomizu Temple
Rock Explosion
Security HQ

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.140
No, I'm...

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.890
Then, you?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.390
Not me.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.650
Then...

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.730
No, it is not me...

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.360
Don't tell me...

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.320
Bzzt.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.240
Then who is?!

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.150
She's from a violent squadron, no?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:13.700
Perhaps her looks may deceive?

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.830
Is that right? You should've told me earlier!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.620
No, that's not it.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.790
We came for this...

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:26.460
Kiyomizu Temple Rock Exp... Esp... splo...

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.090
Kiyomizu Temple Rock Explosion!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.010
It's a rock festival.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:37.600
We're here as Maccha Green's substitutes to prevent the festival from being stopped.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.220
All right, let's go!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:43.560
Oh, Captain! The backup from Tokorozawa arrived!

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.360
Backup? Support for the festival?

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.360
No, this kind of help.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.990
Oh, wow, <i>four</i> of you came!

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.450
No, we're substitutes.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.620
People will let down their guard around you. That's great!

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.250
We'll talk details later.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.540
Come listen to the concert first.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.710
Shido, let them ride with you.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.500
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.420
Later!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.430
She's like Masami...

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.890
Thanks for coming, everyone!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.860
Let's keep this up for this year's Kiyomizu Temple Rock Explosion too!

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:30.400
Yay!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.740
All right, last song now!

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.620
I'm gonna do a cover of a song by a legendary rock band...

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.040
A cover of Momiage Hammers'

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.330
"Stones"!

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.670
No way! It's Momi-Ham!

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.300
And she's doing "Stones"!

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:54.800
Momiage?

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.300
Hammers!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.320
It's Shuten!

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.530
And his gang!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.170
What does the infamous Shuten Doji want with me?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.920
I don't remember this being a battle of the bands.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.050
Come with me, Ichijo Misa.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:42.560
I didn't know you were a fan of mine!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.460
You shouldn't carry around such an unlucky item.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.170
It's bad for you.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.710
Put it in the jinxed stones box.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:19.260
I don't need you to worry about me!

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.270
Lights, beam!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.480
You got it.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.160
Oh, my!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.740
The song princess is being kidnapped by a ruffian...

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.620
Be still, my heart!

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:49.500
Huh?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.250
The hell is this?!

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:51.750
DESTINATION
DESTINATION

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.380
Okay, and go.
DESTINATION
DESTINATION

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:53.880
Okay, and go.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.500
Huh? What? What?

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.510
Mt. Oe
Mt. Oe

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:05.050
No, wait, put me down! Hey!

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.850
It's best to arrive and leave empty-handed.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.560
Captain!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:25.200
Shuten and his hooligans have taken up residence on Mount Oe.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:29.700
They ran wild for us in the meat-and-potato-stew fight with Hiroshima,

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:34.210
but next thing we knew, they had struck a deal with the devil and ran wild in the city as well.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.960
We had an inkling they might target the festival, so we were ever wary.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.970
I had no idea they would go as far as kidnapping the captain.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:46.180
She's the only Best we have, so we're counting on you!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.680
Please bring her back!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.140
Please!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.640
Well, um...

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.020
We're...

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.690
What's that?

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.690
Hey! Come out, Shuten Doji!

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.780
You won't get away with this!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.580
We have four Bests, so don't force our hand!

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.040
Just return our captain!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.700
Did that get through your thick skull?!

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.670
We're counting on you, Tokorozawa squadron!

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.460
N-Nozomi...

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.760
We already <i>told you </i>we can't!

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.340
Give their captain back!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.890
Sure.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.890
As long as you help me kill some time.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:37.900
I just need that stone!

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.190
Cover me, you guys!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.820
Surround them!

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:42.440
Huh?!

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:45.110
While you do that, I'll get the stone!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.320
Cover you, <i>how</i>?!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.330
Here I go!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.330
One down!

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.670
I'll go ask them!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.710
Are you all right, Nozomi—

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:01.630
Something's not quite right.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.960
There's still one more...

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.220
These guys aren't Bests!

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.600
Is it over already? See ya.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.520
You, there. Halt!

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:21.360
Mr Shuten, return the captain of the Kamogawa Rockr's!

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.730
Maikos, We Are?

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:24.820
You came, huh?

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.030
What if I refuse?

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.450
Then you leave me no alternative!

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.380
This is not what I expected!

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.470
I did not think this was how you operated.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:55.350
Sure is nice of you to come save someone you can't even speak to.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.980
That is neither here nor there!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.440
Oh, come now. It was just a joke.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.730
Hey!

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.860
Hurry up and get this thing off of me!

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.110
Captain!

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.710
Let's have some fun.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.590
Life is just about killing time, anyway.

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:41.150
Maikos, We Are is the state vigilante squad

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.730
that protected all of Kyoto during the war between states.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:47.570
Its members consist solely of maikos.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:50.950
Their ranks range from apprentices to those about to become geisha.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.160
The current captain is the 19th Mamechiyo.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.410
Why are they even trying to help?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.410
They only ever look down their noses at us.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.370
What do you mean?

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:04.250
We do not get along.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:07.250
Our captains hate each other.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:12.300
Ours won't even look at theirs,
while theirs can't stop harassing ours.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.100
Something must have happened, but we do not know what.

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:24.650
Yo! Y'all spreadin' the love?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.150
Hello, sir!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:26.980
Huh?!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.530
Sheena, baby, missed ya!

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.650
Hey, old man! Start with me!

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.820
Oh? Johnny, where's Misa?

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:36.280
Well...

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.080
Shuten Doji did it?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:38.740
Yes.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:42.500
We were just about to go try saving her again.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.880
Hey, Nozomi, isn't that Han and Ma from Momi-Ham?
We don't want to be indebted to Maikos, We Are...

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.590
Yeah. We'll get them back ourselves, no matter what!
Hey, Nozomi, isn't that Han and Ma from Momi-Ham?

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.380
Huh?
Yeah. We'll get them back ourselves, no matter what!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.300
Look at those sideburns.
Yeah. We'll get them back ourselves, no matter what!

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:49.710
But why did the Maikos come, anyway?
Look at those sideburns.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.510
Their faces look similar, too...
But why did the Maikos come, anyway?

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.800
What, you guys like Momi-Ham?

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.890
Former Momiage Hammers, Han and Ma

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:06.190
started a record label in Kyoto and they come by every year to help with the festival.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.940
Thank you very much!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:11.740
Um, is the vocalist, Momizo, doing well?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.320
Hush, we don't talk about that.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.870
Don't you know why Momi-Ham broke up?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.910
They had hammer differences, right?

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.040
Momizo was the only one who shaped his sideburns into pickaxes...

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:30.090
They haven't let it go.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.840
A fan would know well to avoid the subject.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.220
Well, what're y'all gonna do?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.180
Huh?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.850
You can hit Mount Oe now,

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.430
but then ya won't finish prepping for the festival, yeah?

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:46.060
'Sides, ya still need to replace the band members being babies at the hospital.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:50.860
If the Maikos, We Are are taking action, can't ya just leave it to 'em?

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.190
We don't want to owe them anything...

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:54.950
Excuse me!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:17:00.120
We'll do something, so please focus on preparations for the festival!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.540
What exactly will you do?

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:04.120
Um... Um...

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.580
You don't even have a plan?

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.420
Oh yeah! Hey, the stone!

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:12.960
Give us the stone that's supposed to be the payment for this job first!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.680
I've finally caught up to them.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.220
Miss Chiaya passed the checkpoint yesterday.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:24.980
Looking at her customs clearance history,
she appears to be traveling with those three...

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.020
The Rest girls who don't seem to be able to do anything

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.610
even though they call themselves substitutes for Maccha Green...

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:31.230
Misono Haruka
Misono Haruka
President of Tokorozawa
President of Tokorozawa

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:35.280
If that's the case, then they should be with the Kamogawa Rockr's in Kyoto.
